 "raw_reply": "{\"item\": \"S442-020\", \"clauses\": {\"determine_value\": {\"verdict\": \"PRODUCIBLE\", \"family\": \"F10\", \"template\": \"Determine the total value of {desc}:\", \"reasoning\": \"F10 asks the learner to determine the total value of a described pile of bills and coins, which is the clause's task. Its desc slot is nested learner text from F14, F15 and F16.\"}, \"number_of_bills\": {\"verdict\": \"PRODUCIBLE\", \"family\": \"F14\", \"template\": \"{count} {face} {unit}\", \"reasoning\": \"F14 prints a count of one denomination with the unit bill or bills, so it produces problems naming a number of bills. F14 is also listed in failing_families for the reasons given under overall, so this entry names the producing family without endorsing its printed text.\"}, \"number_of_coins\": {\"verdict\": \"PRODUCIBLE\", \"family\": \"F14\", \"template\": \"{count} {face} {unit}\", \"reasoning\": \"F14 prints a count of one denomination with the unit coin or coins, so it produces problems naming a number of coins. F14 is also listed in failing_families for the reasons given under overall, so this entry names the producing family without endorsing its printed text.\"}, \"excluding_centavo_coins\": {\"verdict\": \"PRODUCIBLE\", \"family\": \"F17\", \"template\": \"₱{denom}\", \"reasoning\": \"The denom domain for F17 is the fixed set 1, 10, 20, 5, 50 (peso values only), so every amount a problem prints excludes centavo coins. F17 is the family whose values show the exclusion; it is also nested in F14, which is listed in failing_families.\"}, \"up_to_100\": {\"verdict\": \"PRODUCIBLE\", \"family\": \"F03\", \"template\": \"The total is {peso_label}{total}.\", \"reasoning\": \"The total slot repeats the generated total with printed_runs reaching 100, so F03 prints totals across the range up to 100 inclusive. F03 appears in hints.\"}}, \"failing_families\": [\"F06\", \"F08\", \"F09\", \"F14\"], \"failing_templates\": [\"The dot is at ₱{a} and it moves {direction} ₱{b}. Which amount will the dot land on?\", \"Use coins and bills to make exactly ₱{total}.\", \"{stem} Use the fewest pieces possible.\", \"{count} {face} {unit}\"], \"overall\": \"FAIL\", \"reasoning\": \"F14 (template \\\"{count} {face} {unit}\\\"): the face slot draws from F17 (peso values 1, 10, 20, 5, 50) and the unit slot draws from the generator's own list bill, bills, coin, coins, with no tie between them. Its domains therefore allow a problem to show a peso value with a unit it cannot take in the Philippine currency, and a count of one with a plural unit (or the reverse). These are incorrect statements to a grade 1 learner. F06 (template \\\"The dot is at ₱{a} and it moves {direction} ₱{b}. Which amount will the dot land on?\\\"): a and b are drawn independently from 1, 5, 10, 20, 50 and direction from back or forward, with no guard against the result falling below zero, so a problem can ask where a dot lands at a negative peso amount. The lc is also about determining the value of a collection of bills and coins, and a number-line dot movement is not named by it. F08 (template \\\"Use coins and bills to make exactly ₱{total}.\\\") and F09 (template \\\"{stem} Use the fewest pieces possible.\\\"): these ask the learner to compose an amount from pieces, with a fewest-pieces constraint, under the make_change and give_money variants. The competency asks to determine the value of a given collection and names neither composing an amount nor minimising pieces, so these families build content outside the competency's scope. F02, F03, F04, F05, F07, F10 to F13, F15, F16 and F17 raise no fault of their own; their defects, where they show any, come through the nested F14 text.\"}",
